GTA-AVT research source and experiment reports

This release contains an AVT wrapper and experiment utilities together with
historical GTAirway sources. The four historical sources listed in
code/historical/source_hashes.json remain byte-identical to their source
snapshot. code/historical/provenance.json explains the wrapper differences.

Some historical code descends from NaviAirway by Anton Wang (2022). Its original
MIT copyright and license are preserved in code/historical/NaviAirway-MIT.txt;
see code/historical/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the scope and lineage caveat.

That upstream MIT notice does not establish that every later GTAirway addition
or this entire repository is MIT-licensed. No additional project-wide license
choice is made in this scaffold. Preserve the included notices and review the
applicable permissions before redistributing components under a new license.

Dataset rights are separate. AVT data are obtained from their official Figshare
record and underlying collections; no images or dataset license are included.

This repository includes completed AVT experiment reports, prospective protocols
and source-bound engineering records. Each report identifies its scope and
limitations; implemented or checked candidates are not necessarily validated
methods. No trained weights are included.
